module gunbc.non_fold_residue

import std.dissolution { DissolutionCondition, unbound_dissolution }
import std.roster_frontier { FrontierRow, PathSubject }
import std.types { List }
// Shared NFR class strings live once here. Owned subject modules that are not
// seed-mirrored hold `data non_fold_residue_frontier` beside the sites (PathSubject
// names only the symbol; the host file is the path prefix) and import these names.
// Two observing-layer exceptions live in this file's `non_fold_residue_frontier`
// list (one authority: the rows): (1) seed-mirrored subjects, so stage0 rust does
// not compile the audit lists; (2) every `dag/extdeps/` and `src/v2/extdeps/`
// subject — coverage is a receipt in this layer, not a fact of the observed upstream
// (DESIGN §3 external upstream decomposition; those two directories are
// `gunbc.source_layout` trees, not a second path roster). Membership is the host
// union (`non_fold_residue_identity_join_triples`).
// Discovery: the host reader walks production `.dag` files whose source mentions the
// data name, parses them, and keeps the exact `data non_fold_residue_frontier` item.
// The floor's per-diff typed verdict (`non_fold_residue_diff_verdict`) was deleted
// with `run_required_floor`. Membership is still the host union
// (`non_fold_residue_identity_join_triples`).
// Detection-only: never auto-delete rows — greening a site deletes its row by hand with the
// receipt on the PR. v1 seed-reader change is admissible because it unblocks residue
// burn-down for the v2 program.

data nfr_reason_land_red_era: String = "landed unrostered while the gate was red during the land-red-with-local-proof era (revoked 2026-07-12); declared so the ratchet re-arms"

data nfr_dissolve_owning_fold: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "the owning file's fold migration totals the match and the row deletes")

data nfr_reason_typed_census_ca5ed1724b: String = "a top-level wildcard arm over a closed coproduct found by the whole-corpus TYPED census at main ca5ed1724b (#12610's joint landing; nfr_whole_corpus_typed_census, srv1, 2026-10-02). The typed walk keys on the scrutinee's inferred type, so it sees the local-binding, field and call scrutinees the deleted parameter-keyed scan never could; these sites predate the walk and are un-migrated modeling (DESIGN §6), rostered so the ratchet arms at unrostered=0"

data nfr_reason_landed_after_typed_census: String = "a top-level wildcard arm over a closed coproduct that landed on main after the ca5ed1724b typed census, while that census's roster was still in review (#12980); the floor's diff-scoped typed walk named it on the roster PR's own run. Un-migrated modeling (DESIGN §6), rostered so the ratchet stays armed at unrostered=0"

data nfr_reason_trait_derive_shape_table: String = "trait-shape→derive-trait capability table (nested match on ReprGroundingDeriveElemShape × ReprGroundingDeriveTrait with off-trait wildcard arms returning false) landed with Gate-1 sub-wall #2 predicate scaffold (#7174); surfaced by whole-corpus nfr receipt after affected-set predict-skipped corpus-read witness at landing"

data nfr_reason_binding_outcome_resolution_wildcard: String = "StructuralBindingResolution admission projection (StructuralBindingResolved arm extracts binding_outcome; off-variant wildcard Absent collapses six typed index-build refusal variants into option-absence) landed with N3-A carrier move (#7772); un-migrated modeling at assess_reference_binding_observation — the carrier distinguishes refusals but binding_outcome_from_resolution still absorbs them; declared at landing so the ratchet re-arms"

data nfr_dissolve_binding_outcome_resolution_wildcard: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "THE TRIGGER IS A CAPABILITY, NOT AN ARTIFACT: a declaration ref cannot name an arm that does not exist yet, and binding to a fabricated constructor is the DESIGN §3 fabricated-citation class. THE CAPABILITY: gunbc.namespace_cut.namespace_reference_derived_closure_admission ReferenceDerivedClosureAdmission gains an arm whose payload is the StructuralBindingResolution refusal cause — the six closed off-Resolved variants std.reference_binding_observation already distinguishes (StructuralBindingIndexTransportRefused, StructuralBindingIndexModulePathRefused, StructuralBindingIndexExposureRefused, StructuralBindingIndexAuthoredOrderRefused, StructuralBindingIndexDeclarationBucketRefused, StructuralBindingProductionRefused) — so a program matches the cause rather than option-absence. SUFFICIENT FOR: assess_reference_binding_observation routes each of those variants to a distinct assessment without Absent collapse, binding_outcome_from_resolution becomes a total match, and this row deletes with the wildcard. CONSUMERS ARE NOT LISTED HERE (DESIGN §6: name the instrument, never transcribe its output; DESIGN §3c: a declaration's consumers are already a fact of the namespace tree). The producer that re-derives the dependent set is v2.lens.module_impact_query DependentsOf over ModuleIdentity { name: gunbc.namespace_cut.namespace_reference_derived_closure_admission }. The v1 seed mirror of that same module is the emitted file whose path follows the module name (src/v1/stage0/src/gunbc_namespace_cut_namespace_reference_derived_closure_admission.rs); its dependents are that file's, not a second hand census.")

data nfr_reason_variant_test_predicate: String = "variant-test predicate (R1): a match whose arms answer true/false (or none/Present) from the scrutinee's constructor alone, with at most a field condition on the one named arm, and one wildcard for every other constructor. Found unrostered by the row-to-wildcard identity measurement at main 8f00f69fd5b7 (fallback_arm_census_facts joined to the frontier union, Charter 3; measured once, not gated). The wildcard is what makes a newly added constructor answer the default silently; un-migrated modeling (DESIGN section 6), rostered so the ratchet counts it"

data nfr_dissolve_derived_variant_test: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "THE TRIGGER IS A CAPABILITY, NOT AN ARTIFACT: a derived constructor test (`x is V`, realized from the closed coproduct's declared constructors through ConstructorTag promoted to std) is sufficient for each of these predicates to be authored as data over the declaration, so adding a constructor to the coproduct changes the predicate's answer correctly with no edit. SUFFICIENT FOR: the predicate body is that test (plus its field condition where one exists) and carries no wildcard; the row deletes with the wildcard.")

data nfr_reason_one_variant_projection: String = "one-variant projection or pass-through: a match that extracts the payload of one constructor (or rewrites one or two constructors) and answers a default or the scrutinee itself through one wildcard for every other constructor. Found unrostered by the row-to-wildcard identity measurement at main 8f00f69fd5b7 (Charter 3; measured once, not gated). Each other constructor is absorbed into the default without being named; un-migrated modeling (DESIGN section 6), rostered so the ratchet counts it"

data nfr_dissolve_derived_variant_projection: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "THE TRIGGER IS A CAPABILITY: a derived per-constructor payload projection (an Optional-typed read of one constructor's declared field, derived from the coproduct declaration) is sufficient for a one-variant extraction to be authored as data, and a pass-through default is then an explicit total case rather than a wildcard. SUFFICIENT FOR: the function body reads through that projection or a total match and carries no wildcard; the row deletes with it.")

data nfr_reason_wildcard_found_by_join_measurement: String = "a top-level wildcard arm over a closed coproduct found unrostered by the row-to-wildcard identity measurement at main 8f00f69fd5b7 (fallback_arm_census_facts joined to the frontier union, Charter 3; measured once, not gated). It is not a variant-test predicate or a one-variant projection: its wildcard absorbs several constructors into one answer inside a larger fold. Un-migrated modeling (DESIGN section 6), rostered so the ratchet counts it"

data nfr_reason_scores_equal_ratio: String = "DELIBERATE, not structural: UnitCostScore equality is ratio equality (cost over accepted work, decided by two cross-multiplied unit_cost_beats comparisons that must both be false), so UnitCostScore { cost: 2, accepted: 1 } equals { cost: 4, accepted: 2 }. A derived structural == would answer false for those, so scores_equal does not dissolve to ==; its other arms (NetValueScore by micro count, UnboundedUnitCost with itself) and the off-constructor wildcards are the cross-constructor false cases"

data nfr_dissolve_scores_equal_ratio: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "THE TRIGGER IS A CAPABILITY: ValuedObjectiveScore declares its declared equality (a quotient/normalized key for UnitCostScore) so the score equality is the derived == over that declared key and scores_equal deletes with this row; or the incumbent comparison is totalized over a normalized score so equality is no longer asked of two unnormalized ratios")

data nfr_reason_nat_keyed_lookup_table: String = "a Nat-keyed lookup table authored as a match: each arm is one header pin number from the cited Supermicro H11SSL manual and the wildcard answers Absent for a pin number the board does not have. The scrutinee is the open Nat domain, so the wildcard is the declared no-such-pin answer, not an absorbed constructor; found by the row-to-wildcard identity measurement at main 8f00f69fd5b7 (Charter 3; measured once, not gated) because the census treats Nat as a coproduct. Rostered in this layer because dag/extdeps/ subjects are coverage receipts, not facts of the observed upstream"

data nfr_dissolve_nat_keyed_lookup_table: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "THE TRIGGER IS A CAPABILITY: the pin table is authored as keyed data rows (pin number to signal, one row each) read by a keyed lookup that returns Absent for a missing key, so the board's pin map is rows and not a match; or the typed census classifies a Nat scrutinee as an open domain and no longer reports it")

data nfr_reason_wildcard_landed_after_join_measurement: String = "a top-level wildcard arm over a closed coproduct found unrostered by the row-to-wildcard identity measurement re-run on the merge of main eed4a900e23e into the join-data branch (fallback_arm_census_facts joined to the frontier union; measured, not gated); it landed on main after the 8f00f69fd5b7 measurement. Un-migrated modeling (DESIGN section 6), rostered so the ratchet counts it"
data nfr_reason_wildcard_found_by_native_census: String = "a top-level wildcard arm over a closed coproduct found unrostered by the native nfr-wildcard-census (gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:nfr-wildcard-census) over the roster union at the head of its first exact-head run. Un-migrated modeling (DESIGN section 6), rostered so the ratchet counts it"

